# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependencies

### 2. Configuration
Modified `/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart) for Next.js App Router:

1. **Framework Detection**: Identified this as a Next.js 16.2.7 App Router project
2. **Package Manager**: Used npm (detected via package-lock.json)
3. **Component Placement**: Added Analytics component in the root layout (`app/layout.tsx`) inside the body element, following the recommended pattern for App Router projects
4. **Code Preservation**: Maintained all existing imports, metadata, and component structure

## Verification Steps Completed

✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ Linter passed with no issues
✓ TypeScript compilation successful
✓ No test suite detected in package.json (no tests to run)

## Next Steps (Manual)

To complete the setup and view analytics data:

1. **Enable in Vercel Dashboard**: 
   - Navigate to your project's Analytics section in the Vercel dashboard
   - Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
   - This will add routes at `/_vercel/insights/*` after deployment

2. **Deploy**: 
   - Deploy this branch to Vercel
   - After deployment, check the browser Network tab for requests from `/<unique-path>/view`

3. **View Data**: 
   - Analytics data will become available in the dashboard after several days of visitor activity
   - Advanced filtering and custom events are available on Pro and Enterprise plans

